{
  "_comment": "CONSUMER REGISTRY for send_telegram.sh alert ids (OPS-ALERT-RECOVERY-NOTICE-W1 CH2). CLAUDE.md: a shared primitive used by >=2 hosts gets a registry naming every installation \u2014 DETECTION IS STRICTLY WEAKER THAN ENUMERATION. An alert_id firing from a canary nobody listed is exactly what this file exists to make impossible.",
  "_announce_resolution_semantics": "FALSE is the default and it is the LAW's default: CLAUDE.md holds that recovery CHATTER is noise and silent recovery with forensics in logs is the norm. TRUE opts a single alert into ONE bounded RESOLVED message per episode \u2014 emitted only on FIRING->CLEAR, only when a fire was actually DELIVERED, cooldown-exempt, and self-limiting because it removes the marker. Every failure mode of this lookup (absent file, absent row, malformed JSON, no python3) resolves to SILENT, so the default survives the mechanism breaking.",
  "_adopted_vs_announce": "`adopted` = the owner calls --clear on its healthy path at all. `announce_resolution` = that clear is announced rather than silent. They are separate on purpose: an owner may adopt --clear purely for the state hygiene (so a stale marker cannot pin the operator's view) without adding a message.",
  "_unadopted_behaviour": "Every row with adopted=false behaves EXACTLY as before this wave \u2014 same gates, same order, same log verbs, same exit codes. Adoption is opt-in and byte-identical until opted in.",
  "_known_divergence": "The autonomous-optimizer repo vendors its own copy of send_telegram.sh at monitoring/aoe-host/send_telegram.sh, pinned by its own test to CANONICAL_SHA256 243ba4a7... \u2014 which is NOT the live canonical. PRE-EXISTING at the time of this wave (the aoe-1 HOST runs canonical, the AOE REPO's vendored copy is two revisions behind) and deliberately not changed here. Recorded rather than silently tolerated; re-vendoring is OPS-AOE-WRAPPER-REVENDOR-W{NEXT}.",
  "_generated_by": "OPS-ALERT-RECOVERY-NOTICE-W1 CH2 \u2014 union of source call sites and on-disk markers on both hosts, 2026-08-21. NEITHER SOURCE IS COMPLETE ALONE, measured three ways: 14 ids had a live cooldown marker and no discoverable call site; 4 more (incl. the lowercase `gate-shadow-cpu`) had a call site through a $WRAPPER variable and had NEVER fired, so no marker existed either \u2014 those 4 were invisible until the gate's own prove-it-can-fail step exposed the extractor's blind spot. This is the enumeration-beats-detection argument, measured rather than asserted.",
